Here is the audit of `ProductCatalogTests.cs`.

---

## Summary

**10 tests analysed · 7 Critical · 2 Medium · 1 Low**

This suite is a textbook **coverage-touching** test class. Every public method on `ProductCatalog` is called, producing ~95% line coverage, but **7 of 10 tests contain zero meaningful assertions**. Bugs in price calculation, CSV formatting, search filtering, and deletion would all slip through undetected.

---

## 🔴 Critical — False Confidence

### 1. Coverage-Touching Pattern (systemic)

The entire class methodically calls every public method with no or trivial assertions. This is the #1 reason bugs escape to production despite high coverage numbers.

**Tests with NO assertions at all (4 tests):**

| Line | Method | What it skips verifying |
|------|--------|------------------------|
| 17 | `AddProduct_Works` | Never checks the product was actually stored |
| 33 | `UpdatePrice_Works` | Never checks the price actually changed |
| 39 | `RemoveProduct_Works` | Never checks the product was actually deleted |
| 64 | `GetProductCount_Works` | Never checks count value — not even `IsNotNull` |
| 68 | `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` | Never checks prices were reduced |
| 84 | `ImportFromCsv_Works` | Never checks any product was imported |

**Tests with only trivial `Assert.IsNotNull` (3 tests):**

| Line | Method | Problem |
|------|--------|---------|
| 25 | `GetProduct_Works` | Asserts `result != null` but never checks Sku, Name, or Price |
| 54 | `SearchProducts_Works` | Asserts `results != null` but never checks count or content |
| 57 | `GetAllProducts_Works` | Asserts `all != null` but never checks count or content |
| 77 | `ExportToCsv_Works` | Asserts `csv != null` but never checks the actual CSV content |

**Concrete fixes:**

```csharp
// ❌ AddProduct_Works (line 17) — no assertion
_catalog.AddProduct(product);

// ✅ Fix
_catalog.AddProduct(product);
var retrieved = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNotNull(retrieved);
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", retrieved.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, retrieved.Price);
```

```csharp
// ❌ UpdatePrice_Works (line 33) — no assertion
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);

// ✅ Fix
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNotNull(updated);
Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated.Price);
```

```csharp
// ❌ RemoveProduct_Works (line 39) — no assertion
_catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");

// ✅ Fix
_catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));
